messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 612 and 482?I think the correct answer is: 284984\n', '\n\nTo find the product of **612** and **482**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n612 = 600 + 12\n\\]\n\\[\n482 = 400 + 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n612 \\times 482 = (600 + 12) \\times (400 + 82)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 600 \\times 400 + 600 \\times 82 + 12 \\times 400 + 12 \\times 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(600 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 400 = 240,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(600 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 82 = 49,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(12 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 400 = 4,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(12 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 82 = 984\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n240,\\!000 + 49,\\!200 + 4,\\!800 + 984 = 294,\\!984\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{294,\\!984}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is ']]
