final_output:  ['631,150.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **971** and **650**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 650 = 971 \\times (600 + 50)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 971 by 600:**\n\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 600 = 971 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 5,\\!826 \\times 100 = 582,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 971 by 50:**\n\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 50 = 971 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 4,\\!855 \\times 10 = 48,\\!550\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   582,\\!600 + 48,\\!550 = 631,\\!150\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{631,\\!150}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of **971** and **650** is **631,150**.', '']
