final_output:  ['288,000.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **384** and **750**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nFirst, recognize that **750** can be broken down into **700 + 50**. This makes the multiplication easier to handle.\n\n\\[\n384 \\times 750 = 384 \\times (700 + 50)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 384 by 700\nMultiply **384** by **700**:\n\n\\[\n384 \\times 700 = 384 \\times 7 \\times 100\n\\]\n\nCalculate **384 × 7**:\n\n\\[\n384 \\times 7 = 2688\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply by **100**:\n\n\\[\n2688 \\times 100 = 268,\\!800\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 384 by 50\nNext, multiply **384** by **50**:\n\n\\[\n384 \\times 50 = 384 \\times 5 \\times 10\n\\]\n\nCalculate **384 × 5**:\n\n\\[\n384 \\times 5 = 1,\\!920\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply by **10**:\n\n\\[\n1,\\!920 \\times 10 = 19,\\!200\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add the Two Results Together\nFinally, add the results from Step 2 and Step 3:\n\n\\[\n268,\\!800 + 19,\\!200 = 288,\\!000\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{288,\\!000}\n\\]', '']
