final_output:  ['631,764.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **763** and **828**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 828 = 763 \\times (800 + 28)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by 800:**\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 800 = 763 \\times 8 \\times 100\n   \\]\n   \n   Calculate \\(763 \\times 8\\):\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 8 = 6,\\!104\n   \\]\n   \n   Multiply by **100**:\n   \n   \\[\n   6,\\!104 \\times 100 = 610,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by 28:**\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 28 = 763 \\times (20 + 8) = (763 \\times 20) + (763 \\times 8)\n   \\]\n   \n   Calculate \\(763 \\times 20\\):\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 20 = 15,\\!260\n   \\]\n   \n   Calculate \\(763 \\times 8\\):\n   \n   \\[\n   763 \\times 8 = 6,\\!104\n   \\]\n   \n   Add the two results together:\n   \n   \\[\n   15,\\!260 + 6,\\!104 = 21,\\!364\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the Partial Products:**\n   \n   \\[\n   610,\\!400 + 21,\\!364 = 631,\\!764\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{631,\\!764}\n\\]', '']
